"""Approximate string-value openings and document-initial digit runs.

Spaced opening quotes respond positively after colons and assignments,
especially values of name, command, and description fields. Quotes after
short comma-terminated strings receive a smaller response. Initial decimal
digits, including repetitions of the same initial digit, respond strongly.
A few transparent syntax markers, mock-call assertions, and an initial
Title: label have separate fitted responses. Ordinary words stay at zero:
these rules capture prominent peaks, not the extensive lexical variation.
