The largest responses are to men, women, children and people. Other human
age/gender nouns and their counterparts in several languages respond less.
Spelling fragments of these plurals also respond outside human descriptions,
as do memory/menu/enumeration terms and the plurals questions and problems.
This token-local approximation keeps case and boundary differences, assigns
zero to everything else, and does not predict context-dependent variation.
